# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 8, report all keys as escape codes.
# Under flags 9 (1 and 8), a text key sends an escape code in place of its
# text, and so do Enter, Tab and BackSpace, which the protocol's table gives
# the codes 13, 9 and 127. A modifier key pressed alone is reported, with its
# own bit set, and a text key reports NumLock. RIS sets the flags to 0, which
# is what vtium's reset key does to the shown console, and Enter sends its
# legacy byte again.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report all keys as escape codes, Modifiers, Functional key definitions; ADR-1005 D4, D10 and D13 slice 3
# capability: key-kitty-all-keys
size 20 2
send "\e[>9u\e[?u"
check
reply "\e[?9u"
key a
key Return
key Tab
key BackSpace
check
reply "\e[97u\e[13u\e[9u\e[127u"
key Shift_L mods=shift
key a mods=num
check
reply "\e[57441;2u\e[97;129u"
send "\ec"
key Return
send "\e[?u"
check
reply "\r\e[?0u"
